[36m(TaskRunner pid=57070)[0m Explanation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=57070)[0m There is only 1 possible group: (1,1,1).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=57070)[0m  
[36m(TaskRunner pid=57070)[0m Your Task:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=57070)[0m You don't need to read input or print anything. Your task is to complete the function noOfGroups() which takes an Integer N and an array Arr as input and returns the answer.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=57070)[0m  
[36m(TaskRunner pid=57070)[0m Expected Time Complexity: O(N)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=57070)[0m Expected Auxiliary Space: O(N)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=57070)[0m  
[36m(TaskRunner pid=57070)[0m Constraints:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=57070)[0m 1 <= N <= 10^{5}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=57070)[0m 1 <= Arr[i] <= 10^{5} #Us...[+132 chars]
