[36m(TaskRunner pid=57070)[0m Example 2:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=57070)[0m Input: P = (3, 2)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=57070)[0m Q = (5, 7)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=57070)[0m Output: 5x-2y=11
[36m(TaskRunner pid=57070)[0m Explaination: If we use the formula to
[36m(TaskRunner pid=57070)[0m get line equation from two points we
[36m(TaskRunner pid=57070)[0m get this equation.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=57070)[0m Your Task:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=57070)[0m You do not need to read input or print anything. Your task is to complete the function getLine() which takes the values a, b, c and d as input parameters and returns a string which represents the equation.
